        "title": "chore(autoreview): sync canonical review skill",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- What changed: replaced `.agents/skills/autoreview` with the complete canonical tree from `openclaw/agent-skills@cb06fcfafe0c0ac00eabb97589afec05a8a63469`.\n- Why: align ClawScan with the org default `gpt-5.6-sol` / `high` review configuration, access-only `gpt-5.6-terra` fallback, shared isolation fixes, and canonical drift guidance.\n\n## Scope\n\n- [ ] CLI behavior\n- [ ] Scanner adapter\n- [ ] Judge/profile/benchmark behavior\n- [ ] ClawHub profile proposal at `proposals/<GHSA-ID>/clawscan.yml`\n- [ ] Docs only\n- [x] Release/CI/repo automation\n\n## Security / Trust Impact\n\n- [ ] No security/trust impact\n- [x] Security/trust impact explained\n\nThe canonical skill tightens reviewer workspace, environment, secret scanning,\nnetwork, and project-configuration isolation. It also adds `AGENTS.md` plus the\nrequired `CLAUDE.md` symlink so future edits start from the updated\n`openclaw/agent-skills` source instead of creating a repository-local variant.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `go test -count=1 ./...`\n- [x] `go vet ./...`\n- [ ] `go run ./cmd/clawscan --help`\n- [x] Focused scanner/benchmark/manual proof:\n  - autoreview `--self-test`\n  - Python runtime tests: 26 passed\n  - Python hardening tests: 80 passed, 1 skipped\n  - canonical tree byte-for-byte comparison\n  - `git diff --check`\n  - private-data diff scan\n- [ ] For ClawHub profile proposals: I opened the sensitive report through GitHub private vulnerability reporting, and this PR contains only `proposals/<GHSA-ID>/clawscan.yml`\n- [ ] For ClawHub profile proposals: I did not edit official bundled profile files under `internal/profiles/`\n- [x] Docs site proof (`make docs-site`) or `N/A`: N/A, no docs-site source changed.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Full Go proof was run before the final canonical-only follow-ups: `go test -count=1 ./...` passed, including `cmd/clawscan` (190.069s) and `internal/runner` (165.091s); `go vet ./...` passed. Later canonical revisions touched only `.agents/skills/autoreview`.\n- The runtime split review reported one self-test crash, rejected after direct source inspection showed `getattr(args, \"fallback_model\", None)` and the aggregate self-test passed.\n- The policy-test split review intentionally failed closed on secret-scanner regression fixtures; canonical PR #61 already had clean Sol/high review plus Linux and Windows CI.\n",
